    "question": {
      ":question/id": "60968d68-d809-55b7-83d0-39fffb95cf1a",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=16 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-8.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-8)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-4-(-8)=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{3}=-8$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(4)+(-8)=16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=16-(-8)-(-8)=32.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=32$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-8.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨32,4,-8⟩.$",
